# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# macOS code-signing + notarization for App Preview (Apple ID: Tran Trung Hieu)
#
# Copy this to `signing.env` (same folder), fill the values, and drop your cert
# + notary key into THIS folder. `scripts/build.sh` loads it automatically and
# signs + notarizes during `tauri build`. The whole `.signing/` folder is
# gitignored — copy it to another Mac to build there. KEEP IT PRIVATE.
#
#   desktop/.signing/
#     signing.env              ← this file (filled in)
#     DeveloperID.p12          ← your "Developer ID Application" cert + key
#     AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8     ← App Store Connect API key (for notarization)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Code signing (Developer ID Application) ---
# Export from Keychain Access: right-click the "Developer ID Application: Tran Trung
# Hieu (TEAMID)" identity → Export → .p12 (set an export password below).
APPLE_CERTIFICATE_PATH="./.signing/DeveloperID.p12"
APPLE_CERTIFICATE_PASSWORD="<p12 export password>"
# Exact identity string. Find it with: security find-identity -v -p codesigning
APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: Tran Trung Hieu (XXXXXXXXXX)"
# Your 10-char Team ID (Apple Developer → Membership).
APPLE_TEAM_ID="XXXXXXXXXX"

# --- Notarization — OPTION A: App Store Connect API key (recommended) ---
# App Store Connect → Users and Access → Integrations → keys (role: Developer).
APPLE_API_ISSUER="<issuer-uuid>"
APPLE_API_KEY="<key-id>"
APPLE_API_KEY_PATH="./.signing/AuthKey_<key-id>.p8"

# --- Notarization — OPTION B: Apple ID + app-specific password (alternative) ---
# Create at appleid.apple.com → Sign-In & Security → App-Specific Passwords.
# Leave OPTION A blank if you use this.
# APPLE_ID="hieu.trantrung1204@gmail.com"
# APPLE_PASSWORD="<app-specific-password>"

# --- Auto-update signing (Tauri updater) ---
# The keypair lives at .signing/updater.key (+ .pub). build.sh loads the private
# key automatically; set the password here only if your key has one.
# Generate once: npx @tauri-apps/cli signer generate -w .signing/updater.key
# Put the .pub content into tauri.conf.json → plugins.updater.pubkey.
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD=""
# CI: add secrets TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY (contents of .signing/updater.key) +
#     TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD.
